      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Adaptive Gradient Methods",
          "confidence": 0.98,
          "engine": "pdf"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The generic update rule for adaptive gradient methods can be expressed as:",
          "confidence": 0.95,
          "engine": "pdf"
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "text": "x_{k+1} = x_k - η_k · m_k ⊘ (√v_k + ϵ)",
          "confidence": 0.82,
          "engine": "formula_ocr",
          "metadata": {
            "latex": "x_{k+1} = x_k - \\eta_k \\cdot m_k \\oslash (\\sqrt{v_k} + \\epsilon)"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "where m_k is the first moment estimate (momentum) and v_k is the second moment estimate (adaptive learning rate). For Adam, these are computed as exponentially moving averages:",
          "confidence": 0.93,
          "engine": "pdf"
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "text": "m_k = β₁ m_{k-1} + (1-β₁) g_k,   v_k = β₂ v_{k-1} + (1-β₂) g_k²",
          "confidence": 0.84,
          "engine": "formula_ocr",
          "metadata": {
            "latex": "m_k = \\beta_1 m_{k-1} + (1-\\beta_1) g_k, \\quad v_k = \\beta_2 v_{k-1} + (1-\\beta_2) g_k^2"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "text": "m̂_k = m_k / (1 - β₁^k),   v̂_k = v_k / (1 - β₂^k)",
          "confidence": 0.85,
          "engine": "formula_ocr",
          "metadata": {
            "latex": "\\hat{m}_k = m_k / (1 - \\beta_1^k), \\quad \\hat{v}_k = v_k / (1 - \\beta_2^k)"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "width": 612.0,
      "height": 792.0,
      "warnings": [],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Main Convergence Theorem",
          "confidence": 0.98,
          "engine": "pdf"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Under assumptions A1-A4 (smoothness, bounded variance, bounded gradients, and non-negative cost), we establish the following convergence rate:",
          "confidence": 0.94,
          "engine": "pdf"
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "text": "min_{1≤k≤K} E[∥∇f(x_k)∥²] ≤ C₁/K + C₂ σ / √K + C₃ / √K",
          "confidence": 0.80,
          "engine": "formula_ocr",
          "metadata": {
            "latex": "\\min_{1 \\leq k \\leq K} \\mathbb{E}[\\|\\nabla f(x_k)\\|^2] \\leq \\frac{C_1}{K} + \\frac{C_2 \\sigma}{\\sqrt{K}} + \\frac{C_3}{\\sqrt{K}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "where C₁, C₂, C₃ are constants depending on the problem parameters and algorithm hyperparameters. This result matches the information-theoretic lower bound for first-order stochastic optimization up to constant factors.",
          "confidence": 0.92,
          "engine": "pdf"
        },
        {
